NAME
    mute - mute or unmute one audio channel

SYNOPSIS
    mute <index> <on|off>

DESCRIPTION
    Excludes (or restores) one channel from the final audio mix. The
    channel's own playback/envelope state keeps advancing regardless -
    muting only affects the mix, not the underlying voice. Useful with
    'channels' to find a suspect voice, mute every other one, then listen
    to (or dump) just that voice in isolation.

EXAMPLES
    mute 2 on
    mute 2 off
